<Navigation />
<main id="main-content">
<header class="nm-page-hero">
<p class="nm-page-label">Work</p>
<h1>Posta &amp; Roxom TV</h1>
<p> Two cases that show how media, product, marketing, content, audience relationships, and operations have to work together when a format or company is still taking shape.</p>
</header>
<section class="nm-page-main">
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>Posta</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-label">Podcast company · Buenos Aires and Latin America</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Posta began in 2014, before podcasting was an obvious media category in the region. The work was not only making shows. It was building the product, explaining the format to audiences and brands, developing repeat listening and community relationships, creating repeatable production and distribution, and turning an editorial idea into an operating company.</p>
<div class="nm-ledger">
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Context</span><strong>A format before its market</strong><p>On-demand audio had promise, but limited shared language, established commercial models, or regional production infrastructure.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Role</span><strong>Co-founder</strong><p>Product, marketing, growth, positioning, and business development across the company's development.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">What changed</span><strong>From experiment to regional company</strong><p>Posta built an original catalog, branded audio work, and operations beyond Argentina. PodX acquired a majority stake in 2022.</p></div>
</div>
<p><a class="nm-work-button" href="work-posta.html">Read the Posta case study</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>Roxom TV</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-label">24/7 global live media · San Francisco, London, Hong Kong</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Roxom TV posed a different problem: how to run a live global media product continuously without copying the cost structure and organizational shape of a traditional television network.</p>
<div class="nm-ledger">
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Context</span><strong>Continuous output across time zones</strong><p>Live production, editorial work, real-time data, programming, and recovery paths had to behave like one system.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Role</span><strong>Founding team</strong><p>Media architecture and product operations, including workflows, internal tools, automation, and remote operational work.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">What changed</span><strong>A distributed operating model</strong><p>Studios across three continents connected to shared product, editorial, production, and AI-assisted workflows.</p></div>
</div>
<p><a class="nm-work-button" href="work-roxom.html">Read the Roxom TV case study</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>The thread between them.</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Posta and Roxom TV look like different kinds of media company. The underlying work was similar: connect product, marketing, content, audience, and operations so a shift in distribution or production becomes a system people can run every day.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">That foundation now runs through my work on <a href="ai-media.html">AI-native media</a>: how research, interfaces, workflows, editorial operations, distribution, communities, and decision-making change when AI becomes part of the infrastructure.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">For more examples of what I am building, see the <a href="about.html#products">public product shelf</a>. For the ideas behind the work, start with <a href="essays.html">Writing</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>Bring a concrete problem.</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-copy">A new format, a production workflow that keeps breaking, or a product people struggle to understand: these are useful starting points. I look at the audience, the editorial decisions, the tools, and who has to run the work every day.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Tell me what you are building, what is getting stuck, and what needs to change. The cases above show the kind of work I bring to that conversation.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">See <a href="consulting.html">Consulting</a> for engagement types, typical outcomes, and how to start.</p>
<p><a class="nm-work-button" href="contact.html" data-open-contact="" data-contact-mode="conversation">Discuss a project</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</main>
<Footer />
</SiteLayout>
